1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,964
Before registering a high-resolution
anatomical scan to a standard template,

2
00:00:04,964 --> 00:00:07,446
you must remove non-brain tissue.

3
00:00:07,446 --> 00:00:13,403
Scalp fat, muscle, eyes, and skull exhibit
intense MRI contrast that confuses

4
00:00:13,403 --> 00:00:14,892
registration cost functions.

5
00:00:14,892 --> 00:00:19,360
FSL's Brain Extraction Tool, or BET,
strips these structures.

6
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:28,122
BET inflates a tessellated deformable
sphere outward from the brain center until

7
00:00:28,122 --> 00:00:30,173
it reaches brain edge gradients.

8
00:00:30,173 --> 00:00:33,865
The primary control parameter is
fractional intensity threshold, specified

9
00:00:33,865 --> 00:00:35,096
with dash f.

10
00:00:35,096 --> 00:00:36,736
The default is 0.

11
00:00:36,736 --> 00:00:37,147
5.

12
00:00:37,147 --> 00:00:38,787
Smaller values like 0.

13
00:00:38,787 --> 00:00:42,069
3 keep more tissue; larger values like 0.

14
00:00:42,069 --> 00:00:44,530
7 peel deeper into the brain.

15
00:00:49,800 --> 00:00:53,508
Always review skull-stripped outputs in
FSLEyes before accepting them.

16
00:00:53,508 --> 00:00:58,863
Check the sagittal plane to verify that
the cerebellum and brainstem are intact,

17
00:00:58,863 --> 00:01:02,159
and check the axial slices for orbital
fat.

18
00:01:02,159 --> 00:01:06,278
Clipping genuine cortical gray matter will
permanently erase your experimental

19
00:01:06,278 --> 00:01:06,690
activations.

20
00:01:11,367 --> 00:01:13,518
Start with fractional intensity 0.

21
00:01:13,518 --> 00:01:19,543
5, inspect the frontal pole and cerebellum
in FSLEyes, and adjust dash f when

22
00:01:19,543 --> 00:01:19,973
necessary.

23
00:01:19,973 --> 00:01:24,277
Clean brain extraction is the foundation
of accurate spatial normalization.
